invariant: INV-17
file: gcm_avx512.c
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: gcm_seal_avx512 returns without calling avx512_wipe_registers, so
  the round keys, the keystream, H, E(K, J0) and the GHASH sums the kernel
  ran through the 512-bit registers stay there after the call. Every byte
  it writes is still right, so no vector sees it. The script compiles the
  file for x86-64 and requires the call in each entry, and
  bin/x86_kernels_test counts one call after each call of the kernel.

--- old
    // The kernel's frames lay below this one and its values passed through the vector
    // registers, and the compiler clears neither on return.
    wipe_frame_call();
    avx512_wipe_registers();
--- new
    // The kernel's frames lay below this one and its values passed through the vector
    // registers, and the compiler clears neither on return.
    wipe_frame_call();
